\section{Cache contract}{

A cached \verb{<key>.rds} file is only trusted when it has a sibling
\verb{<key>.fingerprint} sidecar. The sidecar is a small metadata object holding
the digest of the serialized value and a schema version tag. Missing
sidecars, malformed sidecars, unreadable \code{.rds} files, and digest mismatches
all fall back to a cache miss rather than returning stale data.

ACS test fixtures are isolated in a separate \verb{acs_test/} subdirectory while
test namespace mode is active; ordinary ACS reads use \verb{acs/} and never fall
back to the test fixtures. Use \code{\link[=cacs_set_cache]{cacs_set_cache()}} to turn caching on or off,
and \code{\link[=cacs_get_cache_state]{cacs_get_cache_state()}} to inspect the enabled flag, namespace mode,
hit/miss counters, and sidecar status.

Suspiciously small ACS cache hits emit a stale-cache warning. The row
threshold defaults to \code{options(catchmentACS.stale_threshold_rows = 1000L)},
can be turned off with \code{0L}, and can be set per state, for example
\code{options(catchmentACS.stale_threshold_WY = 500L)}. Very small variable sets
are ignored unless they match a known stale shape; that guard is controlled
by \code{options(catchmentACS.stale_min_variables = 6L)}.
}

